  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to Urgent Needs of Internally Displaced People in Northern and Central Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mali continues to face a complex multi-faceted crisis resulting in multisectoral humanitarian needs across the country, particularly in the Northern and Central regions where most of the country&#x2019;s conflict and violence hotspots are found. The humanitarian situation has deteriorated sharply since March 2022 and remains highly volatile with the continued expansion of armed conflicts that trigger large-scale displacements. The proposed project constitutes a key contribution to urgent needs arising from forced displacement in Northern and Central Mali and is composed with the global objective of reducing vulnerabilities and improving living conditions of displaced populations and host communities. The project has a three-component approach to support the Government of Mali in providing lifesaving assistance to populations in need: Firstly, the living conditions of vulnerable households among internally displaced people and host communities are improved through emergency shelter and non-food item assistance. Secondly, the project promotes community hygiene and sanitation as well as access to water among populations in need. Thirdly, capacities in site coordination, management and referral are strengthened at the regional levels to ensure timely and coordinated emergency assistance. Beneficiaries include internal displaced people, subnational camp coordination and management actors, and local host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
